---
// What phux does, shown as the commands and the output it prints. The
// transcripts are captured from a real server; keep them true when they change.
import { docsHref } from "../lib/site";
const agents = ["Claude Code", "Codex", "OpenCode", "pi", "Oh My Pi", "Grok", "fx"];
---
<section class="exhibit" aria-labelledby="exhibit-agents">
  <div class="exhibit-copy">
    <h2 id="exhibit-agents">Know which agent is waiting on you.</h2>
    <p>phux watches every pane. When an agent stops at a permission prompt or a question, its session moves to the top of the list, the sidebar marks it, and <kbd>Ctrl-A</kbd> <kbd>q</kbd> takes you there.</p>
    <p class="agent-names">{agents.map(name => <span>{name}</span>)}<span>any CLI agent</span></p>
    <a href={docsHref("/agents#agent-states")}>How agent state is detected <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </div>
  <figure class="transcript">
    <pre><code><b>$</b> phux ls{"\n"}<mark>web: needs you (1 agent waiting)</mark>{"\n"}<i>api: 1 running{"\n"}infra: 1 running</i>{"\n\n"}<i># or be told, instead of looking</i>{"\n"}<b>$</b> phux agent wait --any --until blocked --timeout 600</code></pre>
  </figure>
</section>

<section class="exhibit" aria-labelledby="exhibit-code">
  <div class="exhibit-copy">
    <h2 id="exhibit-code">Anything you can do, a script can do.</h2>
    <p>Create a pane, run a command in it, read the screen, wait for output. Every command has JSON output and a real exit code. The same operations are an MCP server, so your agents work in the terminals you can see.</p>
    <p>Need to step in? <code>phux take @7</code> gives you exclusive input. Automation cannot type into a pane you hold.</p>
    <a href={docsHref("/scripting")}>Drive terminals from scripts <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    <a href={docsHref("/agents#mcp")}>Give an agent the MCP server <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </div>
  <figure class="transcript">
    <pre><code><b>$</b> phux run @1 'ls /nope'{"\n"}<i>ls: cannot access '/nope': No such file or directory</i>{"\n"}<mark>exit=2 (152ms)</mark>{"\n\n"}<b>$</b> echo $?{"\n"}<i>2</i></code></pre>
  </figure>
</section>

<section class="exhibit" aria-labelledby="exhibit-machines">
  <div class="exhibit-copy">
    <h2 id="exhibit-machines">Another machine is one command.</h2>
    <p>phux sets the other machine up over the SSH access you already have. Its sessions and agents then sit next to your local ones. There is no account and no hosted service.</p>
    <a href={docsHref("/remote")}>Remote machines <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </div>
  <figure class="transcript">
    <pre><code><i># once, from your laptop</i>{"\n"}<b>$</b> phux host add me@mini{"\n\n"}<i># from then on</i>{"\n"}<b>$</b> phux attach mini</code></pre>
  </figure>
</section>

<section class="exhibit product-fit" aria-labelledby="fit-title">
  <div class="exhibit-copy">
    <h2 id="fit-title">One lead. A visible crew.</h2>
    <p>Give a lead agent the outcome. With Crew, it places workers in isolated Git worktrees and visible panes, supervises their missions, checks their evidence, and brings back the result.</p>
    <a href={docsHref("/distros#included-distros")}>Set up Crew <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    <p class="crew-requirements">Crew requires a phux source checkout, a build with native missions, Python 3.9+, and configured agents. It is coordination, not a security sandbox or a promise of unattended completion.</p>
  </div>
  <figure class="transcript mission-brief">
    <figcaption>Example task for a configured Crew lead</figcaption>
    <blockquote>Fix the flaky checkout test. Open a PR. Don’t merge it.</blockquote>
    <p>Workers get their own worktrees and panes. Questions and permission prompts still come to you.</p>
  </figure>
</section>

<p class="boundary">Work continues while the server stays up. A server crash or machine reboot ends running programs.</p>

<style>
  .exhibit { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 6fr); gap: 72px; align-items: center; padding-block: 76px; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule); }
  .exhibit:first-of-type { margin-top: 88px; }
  h2 { margin: 0 0 20px; color: var(--color-fg); font-size: clamp(28px, 3vw, 38px); line-height: 1.12; font-weight: 550; letter-spacing: -.03em; text-wrap: balance; }
  .exhibit-copy p { max-width: 46ch; margin: 0 0 14px; color: var(--color-muted); font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.6; }
  .exhibit-copy a { display: flex; width: fit-content; align-items: center; gap: 10px; min-height: 44px; color: var(--color-fg); font-size: 14px; }
  .exhibit-copy a:hover { color: var(--color-fg); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 5px; }
  .exhibit-copy a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent); outline-offset: 4px; }
  .exhibit-copy p + a { margin-top: 6px; }
  kbd, .exhibit-copy code { padding: 2px 6px; border: 1px solid var(--color-rule); border-radius: 5px; color: var(--color-fg); font: 13px var(--font-code); white-space: nowrap; }
  .exhibit-copy .agent-names { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px 14px; margin-block: 20px 14px; color: var(--color-fg); font-size: 14px; }
  .agent-names span:last-child { color: var(--color-dim); }
  .transcript { min-width: 0; margin: 0; padding: 28px 30px; border: 1px solid var(--color-rule); border-radius: 12px; background: #101316; box-shadow: 0 1px #ffffff08 inset, 0 30px 80px -40px #000; }
  pre { margin: 0; overflow-x: auto; white-space: pre; color: var(--color-fg); font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.85; }
  pre b { color: #7fa88c; font-weight: 400; user-select: none; }
  pre i { color: #8f9a93; font-style: normal; }
  pre mark { background: none; color: #e6c384; }
  .exhibit-copy .crew-requirements { margin-top: 10px; color: var(--color-dim); font-size: 13px; }
  .mission-brief figcaption { color: var(--color-dim); font-size: 13px; }
  blockquote { margin: 16px 0 20px; color: var(--color-fg); font-size: clamp(22px, 2.3vw, 28px); line-height: 1.3; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
  .mission-brief p { margin: 0; color: var(--color-muted); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; }
  .boundary { margin: 0; padding-block: 28px; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule); color: var(--color-dim); font-size: 13px; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .exhibit { gap: 40px; padding-block: 64px; } }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .exhibit { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 28px; padding-block: 48px; }
    .exhibit:first-of-type { margin-top: 56px; }
    .transcript { padding: 20px; }
    pre { font-size: 12.5px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  }
</style>
